Prompt Editor is a text editor designed to guide users through the development of high-quality prompts for enterprise LLM platforms. It seeks to accomplish this by lowering the barriers for creating an initial version of the prompt, acting as a quality gate to enforce structure and adherence to best practices, and support iterative refinement by providing target, actionable feedback. As such, the system supports both novice and experienced users in crafting high-performing prompts.

\subsubsection{Prompt Initialization}
The learned taxonomy, derived from a collection of prompts, serves as a template for future prompts because it describes the combination of essential prompt segments for a new task. \ewu{Jeff: Done because it (helps identify the combination of segments relevant for a new task? or something else?)  that's the goal and how it is achieved is the body of this subsubsection.}. Recent work suggests that LLMs can automatically populate structured templates to generate prompts \cite{Cao2023ASO} with performance equivalent to that of a human. As such, Prompt Editor provides a feature to generate an initial prompt for a user to edit, thus reducing the cognitive barriers required for users to design a prompt from scratch.

Given a task description, a predefined taxonomy \( \mathcal{T} \), and optional additional context features \( \mathcal{C} \), Prompt Editor generates an initial version of the prompt. The task description specifies the intended behavior of the LLM, while the optional context features \( \mathcal{C} \) provide supplementary information about the task, such as descriptions of the input data, to ground the LLM's generation. Using these inputs, the system leverages \( \mathcal{T} \) as a template, populating each segment type with content aligned to the user's task through a separate LLM call. This generated prompt is well-structured, contains all the necessary schema elements in the taxonomy, and is tailored to the user's task. As such, it offers a foundation for users to iteratively test and improve.

